    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always fascinated me—it’s like a puzzle where every piece connects logically. My parents both had advanced education in STEM fields (one with a PhD), so I grew up seeing math as a bridge to problem-solving and critical thinking. Though my vocational diploma doesn’t specialize in it, I enjoy the precision of algebra and calculus because they feel intuitive once understood.", "Why is that?": "I’m drawn to its structure and how abstract ideas become concrete solutions. It’s been part of my hobbies indirectly through coding (computer science) and chemistry, where math underpins everything.",
